  // Directional melee (Mark 2026-11-14). Wind-ups slowed 2026-11-15 (Mark: "if i barely hesitate after the red arrow
  // pops up then i take a hit 100% of the time"): every class's light + chained wind-up x1.22, oneHanded 0.45 -> 0.55 s,
  // heavy and counter wind-ups unchanged. Retimed 2026-11-14 from Mark's Last Oasis footage: oneHanded wind-up 0.45 s,
  // release 0.18 s (Last Oasis ~0.10 s; the sword strike clips bake 0.18), follow-through 0.45 s, a chain ~1.03 s strike
  // to strike (Last Oasis ~1.07 s). Other classes are the spec v0.1 guesses scaled the same way. Scavs swing oneHanded (the club they hold).
  // Every swing: windupSeconds (no damage) -> activeSeconds (release, the only damaging phase) -> recoverySeconds.
  // A follow-up clicked from the last 150 ms of the release through the recovery chains: it winds up when the recovery
  // ends, in comboWindupSeconds (25 % shorter than windupSeconds, any direction); the third chained swing ends in
  // comboEndRecoverySeconds. Held past the light windup a swing turns heavy: heavyWindupSeconds (earliest strike,
  // on release) / heavyActiveSeconds / heavyRecoverySeconds, x heavyDamageMultiplier, staminaHeavyCost in total.
  // A blocked or chambered swing stops on contact and recovers recoveryBlockedSeconds (a heavy recoveryBlockedHeavySeconds).
  // 2026-11-17 (Mark: a scav counter after its block always landed - "from the moment the player knows the attack is coming
  // to when it can damage me is just simply too fast"): recoveryBlockedSeconds x0.55 and counterWindupSeconds x1.5, so the
  // blocked attacker is free ~0.35 s before the counter lands and initiative can be traded back.
  // Square set 2026-11-17 (Mark: "everything should be nice and square so we can add different equipment later on"):
  // one-handed is the table in AGENTS.md *Square timing set*; every other class keeps its original ratio to it, per field,
  // rounded to 0.05.
  // A landed hit staggers the victim hitStaggerSeconds (heavy: heavyHitStaggerSeconds) and interrupts its attack; a
  // blocked heavy staggers the blocker heavyBlockStaggerSeconds; the blocker of a light gets one counter swing that
  // winds up in counterWindupSeconds. Rules that do not depend on the weapon (chain window, input buffer, feint,
  // chamber, turn damage, stagger protection) live on PlayerCombat (PlayerCombat.Exchange.cs).
  // Every edit here also updates combat_timings.csv at the repo root (and testscene1's MeleeWeaponTimingLibrary rows).
